<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">kick</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi> command delivers a powerful kick to your opponent during combat,
dealing moderate damage with a chance to knock them to the ground.

<ansi fg="yellow">Requirements:</ansi>

  - Must be in active combat
  - Cannot be used if special move cooldown is active

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi>
  Kick your current combat target

<ansi fg="yellow">Mechanics:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Damage:</ansi> 40% of your Strength (balanced damage)
  <ansi fg="stat">Knockdown Chance:</ansi> 35% base, modified by opposed skill check
    - Attacker: Unarmed Combat skill + Strength
    - Defender: Combat skill + Dexterity
  <ansi fg="stat">Cooldown:</ansi> 5 rounds (shared with bash and trip)
  <ansi fg="stat">Skill:</ansi> Progresses Unarmed Combat

Kick offers a good balance between damage and knockdown potential, making it versatile
for both offense and tactical control. If the knockdown succeeds, your target becomes
<ansi fg="red">prone</ansi> for a minimum of 1 full round. See <ansi fg="command">help prone</ansi> for details.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help bash</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help trip</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help stand</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help prone</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>
